{
 "_comment": "scoot would trick definitions (trick set of Scooter Flow). input.type: flick | sequence | chain | grab. input.layer: trick (RT + right stick; classic: bare flick) | grab (LT + right stick; classic: RT + flick) | trick_alt (RB + RT + right stick; classic: bumper + flick) | grab_alt (RB + LT + right stick; classic: bumper + RT + flick). flow_dirs = right stick directions in the Scooter Flow layout, dirs = classic layout. scooter_rotation (one or a list): axis steer (whips), bars, deck_roll, deck_pitch, bar_pitch (whole scooter forward / back round the bar: front scooter flip), bar_roll (rolls round the bar with the bars turned: bri, inward), whole_pitch, whole_yaw, whole_roll; on grabs the rotation is held while the grab is. timeline (fractions of the trick): rotate = when the scooter turns, accel / decel = share of that spent speeding up after the kick / slowing into the catch, front_foot / back_foot / hands / back_hand = when they are off, lift / raise / side / forward = where the scooter is held meanwhile (m), bars_turn = bars turned against the deck (bri flips), hand_deck = when the back hand is on the deck (fingerwhip; hand_deck_at rear = on the back wheel, toboggan), pivot = how far down the stem a flip round the bar pivots (the arm holding the bar moves round it), hover = false lets the free hands fly off instead of staying over the grips. Directions are for the regular stance; goofy is mirrored. airtime = air time needed, duration = rotation time (s), cancel_window = landing tolerance (s), chain = repeating or holding the input during the trick upgrades it. short = name inside a combination, family = named combinations (whip + bri + whip = Buttercup).",
